# Local stack configuration. See .env.example for every knob and its default.

# The three Form Builder apps live in one directory as real checkouts. ./apps holds symlinks to
# them, which is fine for the host tools but not for Docker: a bind mount carries the symlink, not
# its target, so /apps inside the container would be three broken links and Fact Explorer would
# discover no apps at all. Point it at the directory that actually holds them.
#
# Relative, not absolute: Compose resolves a relative bind-mount path against this file's
# directory, so `../form-builder-examples` is the examples checkout beside your own clone of this
# repository, whatever you named the directory it sits in. Clone the two side by side:
#
#   git clone https://github.com/IRS-Public/form-builder-examples.git ../form-builder-examples
#
# Keep them somewhere else and this is the line to change — an absolute path works, it just is not
# the same path on anyone else's machine.
TAXPERT_APPS_DIR=../form-builder-examples
